### JetBrains template
# Covers JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio, WebStorm and Rider
# Reference: https://intellij-support.jetbrains.com/hc/en-us/articles/206544839

# User-specific stuff
.idea/**/workspace.xml
.idea/**/tasks.xml
.idea/**/usage.statistics.xml
.idea/**/dictionaries
.idea/**/shelf

# AWS User-specific
.idea/**/aws.xml

# Generated files
.idea/**/contentModel.xml

# Sensitive or high-churn files
.idea/**/dataSources/
.idea/**/dataSources.ids
.idea/**/dataSources.local.xml
.idea/**/sqlDataSources.xml
.idea/**/dynamic.xml
.idea/**/uiDesigner.xml
.idea/**/dbnavigator.xml

# Gradle
.idea/**/gradle.xml
.idea/**/libraries

# Gradle and Maven with auto-import
# When using Gradle or Maven with auto-import, you should exclude module files,
# since they will be recreated, and may cause churn.  Uncomment if using
# auto-import.
# .idea/artifacts
# .idea/compiler.xml
# .idea/jarRepositories.xml
# .idea/modules.xml
# .idea/*.iml
# .idea/modules
# *.iml
# *.ipr

# CMake
cmake-build-*/

# Mongo Explorer plugin
.idea/**/mongoSettings.xml

# File-based project format
*.iws

# IntelliJ
out/

# mpeltonen/sbt-idea plugin
.idea_modules/

# JIRA plugin
atlassian-ide-plugin.xml

# Cursive Clojure plugin
.idea/replstate.xml

# SonarLint plugin
.idea/sonarlint/

# Crashlytics plugin (for Android Studio and IntelliJ)
com_crashlytics_export_strings.xml
crashlytics.properties
crashlytics-build.properties
fabric.properties

# Editor-based Rest Client
.idea/httpRequests

# Android studio 3.1+ serialized cache file
.idea/caches/build_file_checksums.ser

/.idea
*.iml

# Read-only upstream reference: a clone of github.com/openclaw/openclaw kept
# locally for reference. Managed as its own repo (git pull there), intentionally
# NOT tracked or vendored into weyland's history.
nodes/openclaw/lab/openclaw/

# Environment secrets — never commit
.env

# TLS private keys / certs — never commit
*.key
*-key.pem
certs/

# AIDLC — the Method (retired B133) + hand-written design docs
# NOTE: /CLAUDE.md was ignored here because the Method GENERATED it (222 lines).
# Since B133 it is hand-written source (19 lines: @AGENTS.md + lab conventions)
# and the entry point that imports AGENTS.md, so it is now TRACKED like the rest
# of the instruction layer (AGENTS.md, .claude/rules/, aidlc/spaces/*/memory/).
.methodaidlc/
/aidlc-docs/

# AI-DLC v2 workspace (B133) — ignored wholesale (operator decision 2026-08-21).
# This is a solo lab and a fresh clone is not a scenario we design for, so none of
# the workspace is worth carrying in git: not the per-machine bookkeeping, not the
# per-workflow intent records, not the derived codekb stores.
#
# KNOWN TRADE-OFFS, accepted deliberately:
#  - `.claude/rules/aidlc.md` @-imports aidlc/spaces/*/memory/{org,team,project}.md
#    and phases/*.md into CLAUDE.md context. Ignoring them means a fresh clone (or
#    a second machine) starts with no method/rules layer and the affirmed practices
#    are lost. Accepted: the lab runs from one working copy.
#  - The framework treats per-intent records (artifacts + the stage diary) as a
#    stage's permanent, committed audit trail. Ignoring them keeps that trail
#    machine-local only.
#  - The codekb is derived from the code and regenerable; a fresh clone simply
#    rescans, which is the correct behaviour anyway.
#
# ── CORRECTED 2026-08-25 (B146). The rule below was `aidlc/`, unanchored, and it
# was wrong in two separate ways. Found by `secret-files` in the code-scan-suite,
# which flags the tracked ∩ gitignored intersection as CRITICAL on the theory that
# a committed-and-then-hidden file is usually a leaked secret. It reported 12.
#
# 1. UNANCHORED. `aidlc/` matches a directory named `aidlc` at ANY depth, so it also
#    swallowed `.claude/skills/aidlc/` — the orchestrator skill, which line 100 of
#    this very file states is TRACKED as part of the instruction layer. Anchoring it
#    to `/aidlc/` confines it to the workspace directory it was written for.
#
# 2. IT CONTRADICTED LINE 100. That line says the instruction layer is tracked and
#    names `aidlc/spaces/*/memory/` explicitly; this rule then ignored it. The two
#    were written at different times and the later one never reconciled with the
#    earlier. `.claude/rules/aidlc.md` @-imports SEVEN of those files BY EXPLICIT
#    PATH (org, team, project, phases/{ideation,inception,construction,operation}),
#    so ignoring them means a fresh clone has seven broken @-imports and no rules
#    layer at all.
#
# THE RESOLUTION: keep ignoring the workspace wholesale — 84 of the 94 files under
# aidlc/ are codekb stores, intent artifacts and per-machine bookkeeping, and none of
# that belongs in git — but explicitly re-include the instruction layer that is
# already tracked and already depended on. Nothing is untracked and nothing changes
# behaviour; the file simply now says what is actually true.
#
# The negation chain below is verbose because git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded. Each level has to be re-opened before the next can
# be negated, which is why it is `/aidlc/*` rather than `/aidlc/`.
#
# STILL DELIBERATELY IGNORED: .aidlc-clone-id · .aidlc-sessions · spaces/*/codekb
# (derived, regenerable) · spaces/*/knowledge · the per-intent artifact directories.
/aidlc/*
!/aidlc/active-space
!/aidlc/spaces/
/aidlc/spaces/*
!/aidlc/spaces/default/
/aidlc/spaces/default/*
# the method/rules layer — @-imported into CLAUDE.md context, must survive a clone
!/aidlc/spaces/default/memory/
# the intent INDEX only (177 bytes); the per-intent record directories stay ignored
!/aidlc/spaces/default/intents/
/aidlc/spaces/default/intents/*
!/aidlc/spaces/default/intents/intents.json

# Stray secret copies — n8n reads the key from a k8s Secret, not this file.
# NOTE: already in git history — untrack + rotate the n8n key (security task).
nodes/mother/lab/weyland-platform/k8s/n8n/encryption-key.txt

# Uptime Kuma restore backup — contains inline dev-password (basic auth) + the Port
# ingest webhook key; can't be templated and still function as a Kuma restore. Local-only.
nodes/mother/lab/weyland-platform/scripts/kuma-backup.json

# Python artifacts (tool-server + any Python service)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
# Virtualenvs and bench output.
# OBSERVED 2026-08-21: `.venv/` under nodes/mother/lab/weyland-platform/scripts/ existed on disk and was
# NOT ignored — untracked only by luck, one `git add -A` from committing an entire virtualenv.
# PREVENTIVE: `venv/` and `.benchmarks/` do not exist anywhere in the tree today. They are standard
# Python conventions and the failure is asymmetric — an unused ignore line is inert, while a committed
# virtualenv is painful to undo.
.venv/
venv/
.benchmarks/

/.junie/

# B88 per-language lane fixtures — the React and Next.js fixtures are the only two that cannot be
# dependency-free (rendering a component needs React + a DOM), so they install node_modules.
# ~458 MB combined; NEVER commit it. The package-lock.json files ARE committed, deliberately —
# they are what makes the install reproducible, and CI restores from them into a cached volume
# (roadie's pattern: named cache volume + skip-if-unchanged).
tests/lang/*/node_modules/
tests/lang/*/coverage/
tests/lang/*/.next/
tests/lang/**/__pycache__/

# BUILD OUTPUT — ignore it EVERYWHERE, not just under tests/lang/.
# The first version of this scoped `target/` to the fixture only, and the very next `mvn` run
# (B88's java test + scan lanes, which execute IN the repo tree) put 105 build artifacts under
# k8s/flink/*/target into version control: compiled .class files, surefire reports, checkstyle /
# pmd / spotbugs output. Build output is reproducible by definition and must never be tracked.
# These are anchored to a path segment so they cannot match a legitimately-named source directory.
**/target/
**/coverage.out
**/.gradle/
**/*.tmp

# ship-images.sh / CI image pipeline: detect-changes.sh writes this build plan and build-images.sh
# reads it — a per-run scratch handoff (target tag baked in), regenerated every ship. Normally consumed
# within a CI run; a local ship that halts at a gate can leave it in the repo root. Never commit it.
.ci-build-plan
